diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index bd522f3..6853f0a 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -18,3 +18,11 @@
 - For non-multipart requests, `Bots::MessagesController#process_action` sets `request.request_parameters = {}` before `super` so Rails/Rack never attempts to form-parse or JSON-parse raw text bodies (e.g. `curl -d "100% done"`).
 - Raw bodies are UTF-8 normalized, HTML-escaped, and newline-converted before saving as ActionText `Message` bodies; `multipart/form-data` requests with `attachment` use `create_with_attachment!`.
 - Responses: `201 Created` (`Location: /messages/:message_id`), `422 Unprocessable Content`, `404 Not Found`, `401 Unauthorized`.
+
+## Outgoing Webhooks & Synchronous/Async Replies
+- `users.webhook_url` (optional string) is normalized (`strip.presence`), validated as an `http`/`https` URL when present, and cleared alongside `bot_token` on `User#deactivate`.
+- Bot forms (`app/views/bots/_form.html.erb`) expose the optional `"Webhook URL"` input; submitting an empty value clears `webhook_url`.
+- `Message::Mentionee#mentioned_bots` selects active bots that are members of the room (excluding `message.creator`) referenced in ActionText mention attachments.
+- `Room#receive(message)` enqueues `User::Bot::WebhookJob` per mentioned bot with a `webhook_url`, so webhook HTTP delivery never blocks the message creator's request.
+- `User::Bot::Webhook` POSTs `Content-Type: application/json` (`event: "mention"`, `author`, `room` with `reply_to` path `/rooms/:room_id/:bot_token/messages`, `message` with `body.text` stripped of that bot's own `@`-mention attachment, `body.html`, and `link` `/rooms/:room_id/@:message_id`).
+- Synchronous `200` responses with `Content-Type: text/plain` (HTML-escaped with `<br>` newlines) or `text/html` create and broadcast a reply message from the bot; `204` or non-matching responses post nothing.
